      "fact": 1,
      "headline": "The March South",
      "text": "The sound of boots on dry stone was a low, constant grind, like a mill wheel turning. Lord Jon Umber sat atop his grey mare, his face a tight mask of concentration, his eyes fixed on the road ahead. Beside him, Roose Bolton rode in silence, his armor dull and plain, offering no words, no commands, only the weight of his presence. The Umber men, three thousand strong, moved as one body, their banners snapping in the thin autumn air. Glover, Norrey, and Liddle followed in the wake, the banners of the sworn lords flapping against the cold wind. There was no cheer, no song, only the rhythmic thud of hooves on the hard-packed road, a steady pulse that would carry them south to Moat Cailin to join the young King in the North.",
      "pov": "Roose Bolton"
    },
    {
      "fact": 2,
      "headline": "The Long Road North",
      "text": "The cold was a physical thing, a sharp needle in the air. Jon Snow pulled the rein on his horse, feeling the weight of the saddlebag against his thigh. Inside, Benjen Stark’s letter lay folded, the parchment stiff with the cold. Six men of the household trotted alongside him, their breath pluming in the freezing air. Ahead, Ghost moved like a ghost himself, a white blur against the grey sky, his ears pricked forward, sensing the wind before he felt it. Jon did not look back at Winterfell. He looked only forward, toward the darkness of Castle Black, where the oath waited.",
      "pov": "Jon Snow"
    },
    {
      "fact": 3,
      "headline": "The Causeway Clear",
      "text": "The wind howled through the three towers, a low, mournful sound that echoed off the stone. Robb Stark stood on the ground, his hands clasped behind his back, watching the archers in the towers. They were steady, their bows raised, their eyes fixed on the road. The causeway lay empty, the fallen stone cleared, the path open and stark. There was no sound of battle, no cry of alarm, only the wind. The silence was heavy, a weight that pressed against his chest. He waited. The South was far away, and the news had not yet reached him.",
      "pov": "Robb Stark"
    }
  ]
}
